#: ../../guide/lazer-vs-stable.md:1
#: 6f3f9dc3928f4f6f9c8b8e738d65c757
msgid "Lazer vs stable scoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/lazer-vs-stable.md:3
#: d0b11d53edd645fead8ddff744445ddd
msgid "osu! has two scoring systems, and pp is computed slightly differently for each. parsecore supports both via {meth}`~parsecore.Performance.api.Performance.lazer`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/lazer-vs-stable.md:6
#: 00a4ddab7fbd4b03aae229aafc6ccd5d
msgid "osu!lazer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/lazer-vs-stable.md:8
#: 211291a248f948a3950bf4d58fffdd28
msgid "Lazer scores carry richer statistics slider **tail hits** and **large ticks** are judged individually. Provide them for the most accurate result:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/lazer-vs-stable.md:23
#: f243656a250c43b19e11a9738078fad5
msgid "osu!(stable) / classic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/lazer-vs-stable.md:25
#: 2600ef3516654f3a99ceb246c9bcd858
msgid "Stable scores don't expose slider-tail or large-tick judgements, so misses and slider breaks are **estimated**. Passing the legacy total score enables the score-based miss estimator (without it, top plays can be off by a couple of percent):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/lazer-vs-stable.md:40
#: c612038adadb430e9020d62bbc4a99fe
msgid "Which should I use?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/lazer-vs-stable.md:42
#: 5b77000a85244549ab12e4dff29ce424
msgid "Use whichever matches the score you're evaluating. The osu! API tells you which client a score came from; feed lazer statistics for lazer scores and the legacy total score for stable scores."
msgstr ""

